  "rationale": "Modularity=0.624 with 325 communities and clustering_coeff=0.349 indicate strong, well-separated community structure, and the community landmarker distribution is sharply skewed (mean 0.132, p99 0.422 — a ~3.3σ tail), so a modularity-residual view should isolate nodes that don't fit any community. Homophily=0.752 establishes a strong neighbor-agreement baseline, making violations meaningful rather than noise; homophily_violation's landmarker shows the same skewed-tail pattern (mean 0.143, p99 0.461, ~3.1σ), confirming a real mismatch population exists. subgraph_contrast's cheap probe already shows a well-separated tail (mean 0.392, p99 0.741, ~3.3σ) even before the stronger full RWR+reconstruction run, and it covers dense local neighborhoods (avg_degree=37, high clustering) that pure community/homophily views can miss. attr_struct_mismatch shows the strongest relative tail separation of all landmarkers (mean 0.037, p99 0.354, ~4.9σ), and with feature_dim=767 and feature_sparsity=0.659 there's enough attribute signal for cross-modal rank divergence to add a genuinely orthogonal view (attribute-vs-structure agreement) not captured by the other three, which are mostly structure- or neighbor-driven."
}
